          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Since my PhD has ended, I went through a process of unifying my various interests in people, proofs, smart contracts, digital money, and zero-knowledge proofs.
    I took a job with <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001Z/" title="Certora" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001Z/" display-uri="dhsorens-001Z" type="local">Certora</fr:link> straight out of my PhD, doing a mix of formally verifying smart contracts and project managmenet/business development/product development/client support.
    Ultimately, it became clear that <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001Z/" title="Certora" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001Z/" display-uri="dhsorens-001Z" type="local">Certora</fr:link> was not the place that I was going to do my best work, so early 2025 we parted ways.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
    I then took some temporary contract work over the summer of 2025 building, designing, and verifying DeFi protocols (my specific area of expertise) while I looked for something that I can truly sink my teeth into and that would define the next period of my career.
</html:p>
